#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Projects Integration
	Testing sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB where multiple projects are involved.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer3                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer3                           |
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	* I create a postal address for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | OSBDSKOSBDSK                  | |
	| Name   | Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	* I create a postal address for an account with the name "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Los Angeles     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 90013           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Main Street |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the support organization with the code "OSBDSKOSBDSK" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| OSBDSKOSBDSK |
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OSBDSKOSBDSK |
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View ticket after requester on multiple projects is removed from project with no ticket
	Zendesk requesters removed from one project should not have tickets in other projects that they are still a part of affected.

	Given I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with ticket subject "Request Subject" should have the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
#	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I go to My activities
#	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
#	| Subject       | Request Subject |
#	| Status        | OPEN            |
#	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
#	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
#	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
#	| Requester     | OSB Customer1                                      |
#	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
#	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
#	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
#	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: View ticket after requester on multiple projects is removed from project with ticket
	Zendesk tickets by requesters who are part of mulitple projects and removed from a project with said ticket should be updated accordingly.

	Given I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with ticket subject "Request Subject" should have the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
#	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I go to My activities
#	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	When I go to the Organization requests tab
# 	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I log out and log into zendesk as "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I go to My activities
#	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
#	| Subject       | Request Subject |
#	| Status        | OPEN            |
#	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
#	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
#	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
#	| Requester     | OSB Customer2                                      |
#	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
#	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
#	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
#	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: View ticket reassigned to user with a different default organization
	Zendesk tickets that are reassigned to a user with a different default organization should also be reassigned to the default organization of the new assignee.

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with ticket subject "Request Subject" should have the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
#	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I go to My activities
#	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	When I go to the Organization requests tab
#	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I log out and log into zendesk as "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticZendeskAdminPassword}"
#	And I go to My activities
#	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
#	| Subject       | Request Subject |
#	| Status        | OPEN            |
#	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
#	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
#	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
#	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
#	| Requester     | OSB Customer3                                      |
#	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
#	| Organization  | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                      |
#	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
#	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
#	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: View user tags after user removal from multiple projects
	Zendesk users that are part of mulitple OSB projects should be updated accordingly when removed from their OSB projects.

	Given I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	When I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag

Scenario: View user tags after multiple project expirations
	Zendesk users that are part of mulitple OSB projects should be updated accordingly when their projects expire.

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	When I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
